# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# Vercel installs dependencies and runs the build itself, so a deploy only
# needs the sources it builds from — not node_modules (172 MB), not a local
# dist, and not the raw client material the site was cut from.
#
# Careful: as soon as this file exists Vercel stops falling back to
# .gitignore, so everything heavy has to be named here too, even if
# .gitignore already covers it.

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr

# Raw client assets — source photographs, layered logos and the print
# brochure. The web-ready versions live in public/assets, which IS uploaded.
JPGs
LOGO
reference
*.pdf

# Local tooling, never served
scripts
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Logs and local env
*.log
*.local
